WEBVTT

00:00:18.870 --> 00:00:22.200
Thank you for shopping with us.
Take your time looking around.

00:00:23.700 --> 00:00:27.250
Oh, that's cute!
Let me know if you can't find your size.

00:00:27.700 --> 00:00:28.950
I'm OK.

00:00:29.450 --> 00:00:32.700
We provide service with a smile,
even for those just browsing.

00:00:32.790 --> 00:00:34.870
Tell me if you want to try anything on.

00:00:34.950 --> 00:00:35.950
I'm OK.

00:00:36.660 --> 00:00:38.120
Take your time!

00:00:38.370 --> 00:00:40.290
Take your time!

00:00:40.370 --> 00:00:42.000
Take your time!

00:00:43.080 --> 00:00:44.290
Take your time!

00:00:44.700 --> 00:00:47.580
<i>Let me take my time already!</i>

00:00:47.790 --> 00:00:48.790
RAGE

00:01:29.120 --> 00:01:33.080
Your purchase of just a three-pair
set of socks comes to 1080 yen.

00:01:33.290 --> 00:01:35.370
Do you have a points card?

00:01:36.580 --> 00:01:37.450
No.

00:01:37.540 --> 00:01:40.830
With our current promotion,
you'll get double points - a great deal.

00:01:40.910 --> 00:01:42.370
Well...

00:01:42.830 --> 00:01:46.250
<i>What a pain.</i>
<i>I don't even know when I'll be back.</i>

00:01:47.750 --> 00:01:49.870
Would you like to apply for one?

00:01:49.950 --> 00:01:52.410
No, thank you.

00:01:52.500 --> 00:01:53.410
Sorry?

00:01:55.290 --> 00:01:56.950
Would you like to apply for one?

00:01:59.540 --> 00:02:00.410
OK...

00:02:00.500 --> 00:02:02.160
Certainly!

00:02:02.500 --> 00:02:07.250
OK, just fill this out
with your name and email address.

00:02:07.330 --> 00:02:09.160
She doesn't need a card.

00:02:15.450 --> 00:02:16.450
Let's go, Retsuko.

00:02:22.000 --> 00:02:22.950
Puko?

00:02:25.580 --> 00:02:27.700
I work part-time in Japan, for six months.

00:02:27.790 --> 00:02:30.870
Once I've saved enough money,
I spend the rest of the year abroad.

00:02:31.450 --> 00:02:35.540
If I run out of money,
I come home and do it again.

00:02:35.830 --> 00:02:39.580
That's what I've been doing
since we got out of high school.

00:02:39.660 --> 00:02:42.120
Wow! So that's what you've been up to.

00:02:42.580 --> 00:02:43.700
Amazing.

00:02:43.950 --> 00:02:45.370
Not really...

00:02:45.450 --> 00:02:47.830
It's the reason
I still haven't got a steady job.

00:02:48.580 --> 00:02:52.040
But that's so you.
It sounds fun. I envy you.

00:02:52.410 --> 00:02:53.450
Really?

00:02:54.040 --> 00:02:55.620
You have a job, don't you?

00:02:55.950 --> 00:02:57.750
Yeah. I'm a regular office lady.

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.120
What kind of work is it?

00:02:59.200 --> 00:03:00.870
It's a trading firm.

00:03:01.620 --> 00:03:03.290
I do accounting there.

00:03:03.540 --> 00:03:04.910
That's amazing!

00:03:05.700 --> 00:03:08.950
But, then, you've always been
the responsible sort.

00:03:11.200 --> 00:03:14.330
Really? You think I'm responsible?

00:03:14.580 --> 00:03:16.120
Because you're, like,

00:03:16.200 --> 00:03:20.330
the kind who never taps "I agree"
to an app's terms of service

00:03:20.410 --> 00:03:23.000
without reading the whole thing, right?

00:03:23.080 --> 00:03:24.660
No, I don't do that.

00:03:24.750 --> 00:03:27.160
The type who's already
saving money for retirement.

00:03:27.250 --> 00:03:28.080
No, not yet.

00:03:28.580 --> 00:03:31.000
You're the type
who buys three pairs of socks

00:03:31.080 --> 00:03:33.950
because you feel bad for leaving
without buying anything.

00:03:34.040 --> 00:03:34.870
That's true.

00:03:34.950 --> 00:03:36.700
See? You are responsible.

00:03:37.200 --> 00:03:40.660
I guess I might be. I'm not sure, though.

00:03:40.750 --> 00:03:41.660
It's a compliment!

00:03:41.950 --> 00:03:43.700
That's a good thing about you.

00:03:44.200 --> 00:03:46.540
But it's also something
I'm a bit worried about.

00:03:48.790 --> 00:03:50.200
Are you enjoying life?

00:03:51.080 --> 00:03:52.500
I'm not gonna lie...

00:03:53.000 --> 00:03:55.500
You look... pretty wiped out.

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:10.540
FOR THOSE WHO WANT A JOB CHANGE

00:04:17.750 --> 00:04:20.000
I'm so busy.

00:04:23.580 --> 00:04:26.410
Goodness! You look a bit tired.

00:04:26.950 --> 00:04:29.200
Yeah... a little.

00:04:29.290 --> 00:04:32.160
Oh, dear. Are you sleeping properly?
Are you eating?

00:04:33.830 --> 00:04:37.580
Maybe I've been leaning too hard on you.

00:04:38.040 --> 00:04:39.120
Huh?

00:04:39.450 --> 00:04:42.200
I share my work with you
because I trust you.

00:04:42.450 --> 00:04:43.790
Forgive me.

00:04:43.870 --> 00:04:45.080
Miss Tsubone...

00:04:46.250 --> 00:04:49.200
Lately, I've been jogging to stay healthy.

00:04:49.290 --> 00:04:50.120
Huh?

00:04:50.200 --> 00:04:52.660
It was hard at first.

00:04:52.750 --> 00:04:56.000
But I kept at it,
and it gradually became easier.

00:04:56.080 --> 00:04:58.580
Muscles build over time, right?

00:04:58.660 --> 00:04:59.580
Right...

00:05:01.370 --> 00:05:02.500
In other words...

00:05:03.000 --> 00:05:06.290
you haven't built up the muscles
for your job yet!

00:05:07.080 --> 00:05:10.160
There! Keep working hard
and build up those muscles!

00:05:12.700 --> 00:05:16.120
You don't have time to be tired!
We're understaffed right now!

00:05:20.750 --> 00:05:23.790
I can see someone
who could help over there, though...

00:05:26.750 --> 00:05:29.040
That's... his job!

00:05:29.290 --> 00:05:30.330
Oh.

00:05:33.120 --> 00:05:36.120
Man, am I busy!

00:05:36.370 --> 00:05:38.790
Man, am I busy!

00:05:39.330 --> 00:05:42.370
Director Ton,
sorry to bother you while you're busy--

00:05:42.450 --> 00:05:43.950
I'm in the middle of something.

00:05:44.040 --> 00:05:46.660
It pains me to increase
your workload, sir,

00:05:46.750 --> 00:05:48.540
but could I have a bit of your time?

00:05:48.620 --> 00:05:50.450
There's something I want you to see.

00:05:51.660 --> 00:05:52.830
What have you got?

00:05:52.910 --> 00:05:54.160
Thank you very much!

00:05:56.450 --> 00:05:58.500
It's a golf course in Northern Ibaraki...

00:05:59.750 --> 00:06:01.370
with unbeatable prices!

00:06:02.870 --> 00:06:04.080
There's more...

00:06:06.000 --> 00:06:08.250
There's a hot spring on the property.

00:06:11.120 --> 00:06:12.540
Komiya,

00:06:12.620 --> 00:06:14.790
we've got our work cut out for us.

00:06:14.870 --> 00:06:17.200
I think I might collapse from overwork!

00:06:17.500 --> 00:06:19.950
Man, are we busy!

00:06:20.200 --> 00:06:22.700
Man, are we busy!

00:06:22.950 --> 00:06:24.750
Man, are we busy!

00:06:25.500 --> 00:06:27.200
Man, are we busy!

00:06:31.950 --> 00:06:33.830
<i>Lightning, grant me your vengeance!</i>

00:06:33.950 --> 00:06:36.040
<i>Hit my boss's golf club - find your mark!</i>

00:06:36.120 --> 00:06:38.410
<i>Lightning, grant me your vengeance!</i>

00:06:38.500 --> 00:06:40.660
<i>Hit the flunky's golf club</i>
<i>Find your mark!</i>

00:06:40.790 --> 00:06:42.700
<i>Lightning, grant me your vengeance!</i>

00:06:42.830 --> 00:06:45.620
<i>Hit the witch's head as she runs!</i>

00:06:45.750 --> 00:06:47.790
<i>Strike them down!</i>

00:06:47.870 --> 00:06:49.950
<i>Strike them down!</i>

00:06:50.080 --> 00:06:52.250
<i>Strike them down!</i>

00:06:52.330 --> 00:06:57.620
<i>Strike them down!</i>

00:07:02.830 --> 00:07:05.040
OK, back to work.

00:07:11.950 --> 00:07:13.660
Retsuko, what's wrong?

00:07:14.910 --> 00:07:16.000
With what?

00:07:18.160 --> 00:07:22.120
I was just thinking, your grandma
probably looks like you do right now.

00:07:25.250 --> 00:07:27.500
It's my grandma in Sayama!

00:07:28.870 --> 00:07:31.910
Retsuko, don't tell me
you finished all that paperwork...?

00:07:32.660 --> 00:07:34.700
Yeah, I pushed through it.

00:07:34.910 --> 00:07:37.750
Whoa! Responsible...

00:07:41.200 --> 00:07:43.250
That's just what my friend told me.

00:07:43.660 --> 00:07:45.620
Am I really that serious?

00:07:47.660 --> 00:07:48.700
Yeah...

00:07:49.250 --> 00:07:51.200
Serious and reliable.

00:07:52.040 --> 00:07:57.370
The type who reads an app's
terms of service before tapping "I agree".

00:07:57.450 --> 00:07:59.290
My friend said that, too.

00:08:01.330 --> 00:08:03.500
The type who starts saving early
for old age.

00:08:03.580 --> 00:08:05.000
She said that, too.

00:08:08.660 --> 00:08:14.040
The type who buys some socks to avoid
leaving without making a purchase.

00:08:14.120 --> 00:08:16.200
Stop freaking me out!

00:08:16.910 --> 00:08:21.620
Because you're the type who is desperate
to live up to expectations.

00:08:23.750 --> 00:08:26.000
I see. Maybe so.

00:08:26.080 --> 00:08:30.830
The type that self-destructs
from doing their boss's job for them.

00:08:32.200 --> 00:08:35.790
A greenhorn robot caught up
in corporate expectations.

00:08:36.910 --> 00:08:40.660
An obedient corporate slave
who waits in line to die from overwork.

00:08:41.450 --> 00:08:44.290
The fodder fattening up
sweatshop companies.

00:08:45.120 --> 00:08:47.080
Fenneko, I think you should stop there.

00:08:47.160 --> 00:08:49.250
Oh! Sorry. I said too much.

00:08:50.540 --> 00:08:52.290
In other words... Oh, yes.

00:08:52.950 --> 00:08:55.330
It means Retsuko is a "good girl". Right?

00:08:55.540 --> 00:08:56.370
I guess.

00:08:57.290 --> 00:08:59.290
But being a "good girl" all the time is...

00:09:00.660 --> 00:09:02.040
tiring, isn't it?

00:09:08.250 --> 00:09:09.080
RAGE

00:09:18.580 --> 00:09:20.370
<i>Judgment from everyone!</i>

00:09:20.450 --> 00:09:22.620
<i>And you tell me that I'm just a drone!</i>

00:09:22.700 --> 00:09:24.870
<i>Bending over backwards for the boss-man!</i>

00:09:24.950 --> 00:09:27.040
<i>Plain vanilla life 'til the moment I die!</i>

00:09:29.620 --> 00:09:33.950
<i>Team players lose!</i>

00:09:34.040 --> 00:09:36.700
<i>Team players lose!</i>

00:09:38.370 --> 00:09:39.870
That's how it is.

00:09:41.450 --> 00:09:42.410
Probably...

00:09:49.950 --> 00:09:51.950
<i>They always look cool.</i>

00:09:52.040 --> 00:09:54.950
<i>Like working women,</i>
<i>overflowing with confidence...</i>

00:09:55.950 --> 00:09:57.620
<i>I'm just a pushover.</i>

00:09:58.120 --> 00:10:01.700
<i>I could never shine like those two do.</i>

00:10:02.660 --> 00:10:07.290
<i>But then, I can't wing it</i>
<i>like Puko does, either.</i>

00:10:12.200 --> 00:10:13.040
Lucky me...

00:10:13.580 --> 00:10:14.410
What do you mean?

00:10:15.120 --> 00:10:18.160
That girl we just passed -
I was hoping to see her all day.

00:10:18.540 --> 00:10:21.620
My fortune this morning said
yellow would be my lucky color.

00:10:24.620 --> 00:10:25.660
That's nice.

00:10:34.160 --> 00:10:37.450
ARE YOU DONE WITH WORK?
CAN WE MEET NOW?

00:10:37.540 --> 00:10:38.370
BAR

00:10:38.450 --> 00:10:40.370
<i>Cheers! Long day, huh?</i>

00:10:40.450 --> 00:10:41.910
You too!

00:10:42.500 --> 00:10:46.250
Nah, I'm not really tired.
No job and all...

00:10:49.250 --> 00:10:51.620
C'mon, Retsuko. Down the hatch!

00:10:53.120 --> 00:10:54.000
So,

00:10:54.080 --> 00:10:57.410
you know how I have to pour drinks
for Director Ton at work parties?

00:10:57.500 --> 00:11:00.000
So I was pouring the beer like this and...

00:11:02.540 --> 00:11:05.950
You're supposed to pour
with the bottle label-side up.

00:11:06.040 --> 00:11:08.580
Don't you even know that much?

00:11:09.500 --> 00:11:13.120
That is the problem with young women.

00:11:14.950 --> 00:11:15.950
What the hell!

00:11:16.040 --> 00:11:18.830
Right? It doesn't make any sense!

00:11:19.120 --> 00:11:22.870
Didn't old men like that
die off in the '80s?

00:11:22.950 --> 00:11:25.290
Not at our office.

00:11:26.500 --> 00:11:31.000
Sockets have started to remind me
of Director Ton's face.

00:11:32.040 --> 00:11:33.250
That's funny!

00:11:33.500 --> 00:11:38.160
Someday, I want to slap
a resignation letter right in his face.

00:11:38.700 --> 00:11:40.450
That's my dream.

00:11:42.950 --> 00:11:45.200
It's really fun to talk with you.

00:11:46.000 --> 00:11:49.120
Oh, sorry.
I'm only talking about myself, aren't I?

00:11:49.200 --> 00:11:52.620
What are you going to do now?
Will you be in Japan for a while?

00:11:57.200 --> 00:12:00.540
Actually, I was thinking I might
start a business here in Japan.

00:12:01.950 --> 00:12:03.080
A business?

00:12:03.790 --> 00:12:05.910
Well, me and a friend together.

00:12:06.000 --> 00:12:07.250
What are you doing?

00:12:09.080 --> 00:12:10.410
An imported goods store.

00:12:14.330 --> 00:12:17.120
An imported goods store!

00:12:18.040 --> 00:12:20.330
We'll bring back products from overseas.

00:12:20.410 --> 00:12:23.200
I've got plenty of friends out there.

00:12:23.500 --> 00:12:27.000
With our tastes, I bet
we could do something interesting.

00:12:27.660 --> 00:12:28.700
Seriously?

00:12:29.200 --> 00:12:30.660
That's super great!

00:12:30.910 --> 00:12:33.870
Oh, stop it. It's not that big of a deal.

00:12:33.950 --> 00:12:36.750
It is! I am super jealous!

00:12:39.290 --> 00:12:40.370
Well... You want in?

00:12:40.830 --> 00:12:41.750
What?

00:12:43.950 --> 00:12:47.410
Wait a second.
Stop. I just got really shaky.

00:12:47.500 --> 00:12:48.330
Really?

00:12:48.950 --> 00:12:50.160
Then let's do it.

00:12:53.410 --> 00:12:55.700
But I've got the company...

00:12:56.450 --> 00:12:57.790
Why don't you quit?

00:13:02.580 --> 00:13:04.660
<i>Retsuko, you can do accounting, can't you?</i>

00:13:04.750 --> 00:13:07.870
<i>My friend and I</i>
<i>are the happy-go-lucky types,</i>

00:13:07.950 --> 00:13:11.000
<i>so someone responsible like you</i>
<i>would make up for what we lack.</i>

00:13:11.330 --> 00:13:12.330
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:13:12.410 --> 00:13:15.200
<i>You can go overseas to make deals!</i>

00:13:15.290 --> 00:13:16.660
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:13:16.750 --> 00:13:18.120
<i>So? Wanna do it?</i>

00:13:19.370 --> 00:13:22.200
<i>Seriously, seriously, seriously?</i>

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:25.370
<i>Seriously?</i>

00:13:30.080 --> 00:13:31.540
ACCOUNTING DEPARTMENT

00:13:37.790 --> 00:13:39.200
What are you doing?

00:13:41.750 --> 00:13:42.870
Exercise.

00:13:44.950 --> 00:13:47.290
Cleaning and exercising
at the same time...

00:13:49.580 --> 00:13:51.290
Well, aren't you carefree.

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:54.290
I've got the perfect exercise for you.

00:13:54.370 --> 00:13:56.450
Polish my clubs.

00:13:56.540 --> 00:13:58.040
Yes, sir.

00:13:58.120 --> 00:13:59.790
Don't scratch them.

00:14:00.500 --> 00:14:02.950
Man, am I busy!

00:14:03.250 --> 00:14:05.500
Man, am I busy!

00:14:06.330 --> 00:14:07.160
Man, am I busy!

00:14:07.250 --> 00:14:08.790
<i>You're the carefree one.</i>

00:14:08.870 --> 00:14:11.040
<i>This is practice for the near future,</i>

00:14:11.750 --> 00:14:16.290
<i>when I smack you in the face</i>
<i>with a resignation letter.</i>

00:14:18.410 --> 00:14:19.620
<i>I'm gonna quit.</i>

00:14:20.790 --> 00:14:21.660
<i>I'm gonna quit...</i>

00:14:23.120 --> 00:14:24.790
<i>this awful job.</i>

00:14:25.830 --> 00:14:27.580
Well, thanks in advance.

00:14:28.160 --> 00:14:30.620
<i>I'm gonna quit the crap out of it!</i>

00:14:34.290 --> 00:14:36.290
Subtitle translation: John Haguewood
